  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "<div align=\"center\">"
    },
    {
      "section": "evo",
      "text": "**Evolving memory for agents — recall before the model thinks, reflect after it answers.**\n\n[](LICENSE)\n[](https://nodejs.org)\n[](#status)\n\n</div>\n\nevo is a provider-neutral memory service that gives AI coding agents durable, cross-session memory. It recalls relevant knowledge into the system prompt before a model step, and reflects completed turns into structured memory afterwards — so an agent keeps what it learned across sessions without you writing it down."
    },
    {
      "section": "Why evo?",
      "text": "Local CLI agents (Claude Code, Codex, DeepSeek Harness) are stateless by default: each session starts from zero. User preferences, project conventions, pitfalls stepped into three times — all evaporate when the session ends.\n\nevo solves this with a **recall + reflect loop**:\n\n- **Recall**: Before each prompt, assemble relevant memories into the agent's context\n- **Reflect**: After each successful turn, distill the conversation into structured memory items"
    },
    {
      "section": "Why evo?",
      "text": "The result: your agent becomes an experienced colleague who remembers the project."
    },
    {
      "section": "Documentation",
      "text": "| Section | Description |\n| --- | --- |\n| [GitBook Docs](https://evo-5.gitbook.io/evo/) | Primary documentation site |\n| [Getting Started](docs/getting-started/requirements.md) | Requirements and installation |\n| [Host Integrations](docs/hosts/deepseek-harness.md) | DeepSeek Harness, Claude Code, Codex |\n| [Concepts](docs/concepts/how-it-works.md) | How recall + reflect works |\n| [Configuration](docs/configuration/environment-variables.md) | All settings and environment variables |\n| [API Reference](docs/api/http-api.md) | HTTP and service APIs |\n| [Development](docs/development/contributing.md) | Contributing guide |"
    },
    {
      "section": "DeepSeek Harness",
      "text": "```bash\n./install_evo_dsps.sh\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Claude Code",
      "text": "```bash\n/plugin marketplace add TIZ36/evo\n/plugin install evo\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Codex",
      "text": "```bash\ncodex plugin marketplace add TIZ36/evo\ncodex plugin add evo@evo\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Key Features",
      "text": "- **Structured memory**: Every item has a scope, kind (fact, constraint, procedure, skill…), tags, and source\n- **First-class skills**: Procedural SOPs separate from declarative memories, with lessons learned tracking and a dedicated Skills tab in the Memory panel\n- **Batch distillation**: Turns are collected and distilled in batches for better memory quality\n- **Local by default**: SQLite storage via Node's built-in `node:sqlite` — nothing leaves the machine except reflection model calls\n- **Workspace import**: Existing `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `.codex/`, and similar files are imported automatically\n- **Provider-neutral**: Works with DeepSeek Harness, Claude Code, and Codex through adapters"
    },
    {
      "section": "Status",
      "text": "evo is currently **alpha (0.3.x)**. The core loop is stable and used daily, but APIs may change."
    },
    {
      "section": "Current Limitations",
      "text": "- Recall uses deterministic SQLite filtering and ranking, without embeddings\n- Consolidation runs automatically on the slow path (floor 24h / 72h converged, or large replay buffer); call `consolidate()` or use the web panel for manual runs\n- `node:sqlite` is still marked experimental by current Node releases (it ships with Node 22+)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```bash\npnpm install\npnpm check          # test + typecheck + build + rule scan\n```\n\nSee [Contributing](docs/development/contributing.md) for the full development guide."
    },
    {
      "section": "Project Rule",
      "text": "This is a personal open-source project. Company identity and sensitive information must never appear in the repository. Team attribution is \"Paper team\" only. See [Project Rules](docs/development/project-rules.md) for details."
    },
